icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=617627#post617627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Henry the eigth with a leg of turkey does sound familiar...<br /> Damn it, Neal &amp; Wolfgar, you've broken space-time.<br /> All we wanted was a recap of the GenCon panel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha!<br /> <br /> I wished I'd taken some notes now, things are kind of a blur. They mostly just talked generally about some of the books that will be coming out. They didn't get into specifics of the new system or anything. They did say while the 3 games as a whole are called The Trinity Continuum, the game Trinity is reverting back to it's original title of Aeon. I thought that was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I wish now I'd asked some questions about the system though....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T20:52:45-07:00","id":618418,"title":"","content":"* The official name of &quot;Sardonyx&quot; is the Storypath System.<br /> * If I have my way, the words &quot;Aberrant War&quot; will not appear in the Aberrant rulebook.<br /> * I teased a secondary timeline, Anima, which has its own thread.<br /> <br /> That's all the major stuff I can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T04:22:17-07:00","id":618677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=618418#post618418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The official name of &quot;Sardonyx&quot; is the Storypath System.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wish I'd ask a question about the system...not sure why I didn't. Too nervous I guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=618418#post618418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* If I have my way, the words &quot;Aberrant War&quot; will not appear in the Aberrant rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>* I teased a secondary timeline, Anima, which has its own thread.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Oh yea! You did say that! Now I remember...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:46:46-07:00","id":618704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=618418#post618418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The official name of &quot;Sardonyx&quot; is the Storypath System.<br /> * If I have my way, the words &quot;Aberrant War&quot; will not appear in the Aberrant rulebook.<br /> <br /> That's all the major stuff I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, then Where will be advice to play Abberant in Aeon setting?<br /> <br /> p.s. Sardonyx sounds better. From tease I do not remember any storypath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:04:40-07:00","id":618876,"title":"","content":"Okay, apart from the story-path title, this is stuff i feel i've already gathered. I assume it was a kind of short panel, if you are willing to take questions over the forum, i'm certain we could tease out some further details. I probably would have asked so many that security might have been called to escort me out.<br /> -blush-<br /> <br /> I'm still getting used to calling the Trinity 2120 setting 'Aeon' again after so long - i expect to make some confusing gaffs along the way to acceptance. Context is going to be important, as a heads up. I <i>do</i> like that things are too big to really contain in a universe (TU), requiring redesignation as a continuum (TC). Now, if we can just do something about the words &quot;Anima&quot; and &quot;Quantum&quot;...<br /> <br /> I like Storypath, Sardonyx is a cool name but it says nothing about the attached product, Storypath invokes the Storyteller system from the original game and the Pathfinder/Paizo 'update' on D&amp;D 3.5. It sounds like a RPG rule set now and i'm pleased with that.<br /> <br /> Aberrant War should only be allowed to appear in the 'quantum-wibbly' (am i doing this right?) sidebars about continuity and timelines in the Aberrant setting, i can entirely agree with that. There may be some level of foreboding lost, but i've had some minor trouble with players meta-gaming before. Opening up the ending is great news for the game table, but it cuts both ways by sacrificing the timeline of the original settings - which i found to be the most important element connecting the games outside of inspiration mechanics. I have to admit, losing a single congruous history for the 'quantum-wibbly' concerns me a bit, but only because i haven't seen the end result yet.<br /> <br /> I have already addressed Anima elsewhere, but it bears repeating that i have some tonal concerns regarding the setting's similarity to Aeon based from the little we know. Otherwise, i am happy to admit i'm keen to see what the dev team comes up with to cannibalize/utilize as required.<br /> <br /> In reply to Zorb42; i believe the Storypath rules from Aberrant and Aeon will simply be more robust, allowing easier cross-overs and there may be some more consciously placed story hooks for parties comprised of era-inappropriate or mixed inspiration members. I imagine anything more would be included in a follow up supplement - probably not anything too high priority either.<br /> -shrug-<br /> But, i will be reading between the lines for 2120 aberrant PC's myself (old habits) and i've heard nothing so far that directly contradicts anything i did in the past. This reboot may very well see us revisit the characters we had to abandon due to the rules experiencing a kind of BSoD around my table. All i will need to try that is the Aeon, Aberrant and Core books (i think, corrections are welcome) - which i'm excited for.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the information, Gone and Ian. Now maybe the timeline flux caused by <i>some</i> posters can begin to stabilize...<br /> -glowers accusingly at Neall and Wolfgar, narrowly avoiding the Joykiller 3000-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Adjusting for JK-3000 08-07-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:04:54-07:00","id":619006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=618704#post618704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then Where will be advice to play Abberant in Aeon setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aeon-era nova PCs will probably be detailed in an Aeon book, once Aberrant has come out and established the mechanics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T10:32:53-07:00","id":619090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619006#post619006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aeon-era nova PCs will probably be detailed in an Aeon book, once Aberrant has come out and established the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously Ian's been clear to tell us before that plenty of stuff hasn't been decided yet so I take this as 'here's a way we may do that' not 'this is exactly what we're going to do'. Having said that, couple of thoughts on the thread.<br /> <br /> Storypath: I like. The 'story' part is obvious, and I took 'path' to be 'Onyx Path'. I could see how Pathfinder may come to mind, and depending on your point of view that could be a bad or good thing (I doubt OPP are trying to use Pathfinder's arguably mess of a line as inspiration for a production plan). But yeah, Storypath is much better than Sardonyx for me.<br /> <br /> Aeon-era Nova PCs: Seeing this possibly in its own book is a great idea. No, seriously, I mean it, stop laughing! Players &amp; GM's who want to bring Novas into Aeon can get the kind of support that will need. And I can readily ignore it without much effort. Perfect. Love it.<br /> <br /> Taking that idea further, I'd like to see this kind of 'crossover' sourcebook for other things through the Continuum. An Aberrant era book introducing Psions or an Adventure! era book introducing some weird alien race from the Aeon period, for example. Take popular elements for specific game time periods and introduce a book (mini or full, depends on subject I guess) facilitating crossovers in other periods, and they can be used or entirely ignored. This would make my job easier as a GM. Any chance of this kind of thing Ian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 08-07-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T10:37:47-07:00","id":619120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619090#post619090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storypath: I like. The 'story' part is obvious, and I took 'path' to be 'Onyx Path'. I could see how Pathfinder may come to mind, and depending on you point of view that could be a bad or good thing ( doubt OPP are trying to use Pathfinder's arguably mess of a line as inspiration for a production plan) . But yeah, Storypath is much better than Sardonyx for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a specific mechanic called Paths that detail your connections to various organizations, system topics, and how your Merits and Skills connect to the larger setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T11:14:41-07:00","id":619177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619120#post619120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a specific mechanic called Paths that detail your connections to various organizations, system topics, and how your Merits and Skills connect to the larger setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for chiming in Neall. <br /> <br /> Hrm. Have to see how that actually works. My (entirely) knee-jerk initial reaction based on no real information whatsoever is '<i>uh oh, that feels like it could be restrictive / unneeded</i>'. I'll definitely have a read when (if) we get a teaser <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:04:35-07:00","id":619532,"title":"","content":"&quot;Storypath&quot; means a lot of things. Obviously there's homage to the Storyteller/ing System, plus the nod to Onyx Path itself, in addition to the Path mechanic within the system.<br /> <br /> The name also has a <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Path-Intrigue-Story-Paths/dp/0962779024\" target=\"_blank\">pretty long history</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619090#post619090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aeon-era Nova PCs: Seeing this possibly in its own book is a great idea. No, seriously, I mean it, stop laughing! Players &amp; GM's who want to bring Novas into Aeon can get the kind of support that will need. And I can readily ignore it without much effort. Perfect. Love it.<br /> <br /> Taking that idea further, I'd like to see this kind of 'crossover' sourcebook for other things through the Continuum. An Aberrant era book introducing Psions or an Adventure! era book introducing some weird alien race from the Aeon period, for example. Take popular elements for specific game time periods and introduce a book (mini or full, depends on subject I guess) facilitating crossovers in other periods, and they can be used or entirely ignored. This would make my job easier as a GM. Any chance of this kind of thing Ian?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's really enough material for a &quot;crossover sourcebook&quot; to make it worthwhile, and most people wouldn't use the entire thing anyway. We'd be more likely to, for example, include Aeon-era novas in an Extrasolar Space supplement among the information on nova colonies. That's the situation that's most likely to give rise to nova PCs, so it's a natural fit. We'll see how the production schedule shapes up to see where it fits in best.<br /> <br /> If all else fails, it shouldn't be a big problem to just use the nova rules from Aberrant. Novas a century later might have access to a few powers their predecessors don't, but otherwise I don't see that the systems would be markedly different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:49:51-07:00","id":619581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619532#post619532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Storypath&quot; means a lot of things. Obviously there's homage to the Storyteller/ing System, plus the nod to Onyx Path itself, in addition to the Path mechanic within the system.<br /> <br /> The name also has a <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Path-Intrigue-Story-Paths/dp/0962779024\" target=\"_blank\">pretty long history</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Intrigue huh - wow, that's going back a bit. I haven't seen that in a long while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619532#post619532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's really enough material for a &quot;crossover sourcebook&quot; to make it worthwhile, and most people wouldn't use the entire thing anyway. We'd be more likely to, for example, include Aeon-era novas in an Extrasolar Space supplement among the information on nova colonies. That's the situation that's most likely to give rise to nova PCs, so it's a natural fit. We'll see how the production schedule shapes up to see where it fits in best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, gotcha. Fair enough - I suspect I can simply ignore anything to do with Nova colonies in such an example, probably with less work than in the original TU actually. I know this is a hypothetical right now, subject to change and son on though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619532#post619532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all else fails, it shouldn't be a big problem to just use the nova rules from Aberrant. Novas a century later might have access to a few powers their predecessors don't, but otherwise I don't see that the systems would be markedly different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can see that. Obviously that all depends on how all the mechanics shake out, but its good you've got a range of options this time around. Thanks for the response <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:40:20-07:00","id":620060,"title":"","content":"I've been calling the game Aeon forever, because fuck Viacom. So there is no need to shift for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:47:19-07:00","id":620064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the information, Gone and Ian. Now maybe the timeline flux caused by <i>some</i> posters can begin to stabilize...<br /> -glowers accusingly at Neall and Wolfgar, narrowly avoiding the Joykiller 3000- </div> </div> </div>Yeah, man, after all the stuff Neil talked about in the alt timeline, I'm just super excited for the core. I mean we've got the COBRA expy and that one evil international corporation was pretty cool, basically Pentex done right, and that whole cannibal secret society... the whole thing really does just have the &quot;Saturday morning action cartoon for grown-ups&quot; thing happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> I mean, too bad we don't remember any of that stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T07:53:50-07:00","id":633477,"title":"","content":"So now that Gencon has come and gone... Any chance the previews will starting back up soon? Also, I dropped a line to Lone Wolf Productions about the Storypath system. They're the peeps that make Hero Lab and Realmworks. Hopefully you can all workout some support!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T08:21:25-07:00","id":633496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=633477#post633477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now that Gencon has come and gone... Any chance the previews will starting back up soon? Also, I dropped a line to Lone Wolf Productions about the Storypath system. They're the peeps that make Hero Lab and Realmworks. Hopefully you can all workout some support!</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be cool.<br /> <br /> Yeah, previews will be starting soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T10:52:45-07:00","id":633582,"title":"","content":"Here's the link to the thread I started at the LWD forums. A staff member, Liz, says she's open to talking about it with you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=53677\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/data/assets/logo/forums_logo_transparent.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=53677\" target=\"_blank\"> Working for the people/man? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=53677\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=53677 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Is there a setting in Hero Lab for 5ed, that lets those who run or play in missions, select working for the man or people between missions? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T09:14:33-07:00","id":637081,"title":"","content":"Life has been Hell without game previews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:25:33-08:00","id":797017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/616451-gencon-trinity-panel?p=619177#post619177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for chiming in Neall.<br /> <br /> Hrm. Have to see how that actually works. My (entirely) knee-jerk initial reaction based on no real information whatsoever is '<i>uh oh, that feels like it could be restrictive / unneeded</i>'. I'll definitely have a read when (if) we get a teaser <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if it has anything to do with it, but the concept makes me think of Weapons of the Gods' Honestly, Lores &amp; Destinies. Now i'm curious to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}